				</ukm:Metadata><Secondary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/body" NumberOfProvisions="659" RestrictExtent="E+W" RestrictStartDate="2026-10-05"><Part DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/part/30" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/part/30" NumberOfProvisions="9" id="part-30" RestrictExtent="E+W" RestrictStartDate="2026-04-06"><Number>PART 30</Number><Title id="p02898">ENFORCEMENT OF FINES AND OTHER ORDERS FOR PAYMENT</Title><P1group RestrictExtent="E+W" RestrictStartDate="2026-04-06"><Title>Application to reduce a fine, vary payment terms or  <Substitution ChangeId="key-28bc16ac35d32338d54a6afb9d47f6a2-1775737460591" CommentaryRef="key-28bc16ac35d32338d54a6afb9d47f6a2">remit</Substitution>  a courts charge</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5" id="rule-30.5"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-c9768c7929b875915d09db3ebc028657"/>30.5</Pnumber><P1para><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1" id="rule-30.5-1"><Pnumber><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">1</Substitution></Pnumber><P2para><Text><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">This rule applies where—</Substitution></Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/a" id="rule-30.5-1-a"><Pnumber><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">a</Substitution></Pnumber><P3para><Text><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">the defendant wants the court to remit the whole or any part of a fine;</Substitution></Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/b" id="rule-30.5-1-b"><Pnumber><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">b</Substitution></Pnumber><P3para><Text><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">no collection order is in force and the defendant wants the court to vary payment terms; or</Substitution></Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/c" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1/c" id="rule-30.5-1-c"><Pnumber><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">c</Substitution></Pnumber><P3para><Text><Substitution ChangeId="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a-1775737476400" CommentaryRef="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a">the defendant, a fines officer or an enforcement agent wants the court to remit a criminal courts charge.</Substitution></Text></P3para></P3></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2" id="rule-30.5-2"><Pnumber>2</Pnumber><P2para><Text>Unless the court otherwise directs, such a defendant, fines officer or enforcement agent must—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/a" id="rule-30.5-2-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text>apply in writing;</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/b" id="rule-30.5-2-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text>serve the application on the court officer;</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c" id="rule-30.5-2-c"><Pnumber>c</Pnumber><P3para><Text>if the application is to  <Substitution ChangeId="key-a888c5a3fb73f175f11ab7629ff3c204-1775737522228" CommentaryRef="key-a888c5a3fb73f175f11ab7629ff3c204">remit</Substitution>  a fine or vary payment terms, explain—</Text><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c/i" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c/i" id="rule-30.5-2-c-i"><Pnumber>i</Pnumber><P4para><Text>what relevant circumstances have not yet been considered by the court, and</Text></P4para></P4><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c/ii" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c/ii" id="rule-30.5-2-c-ii"><Pnumber>ii</Pnumber><P4para><Text>why the fine should be  <Substitution ChangeId="key-5f8f9fe45bfb0867d2fb21f0b5ddccc1-1775737545439" CommentaryRef="key-5f8f9fe45bfb0867d2fb21f0b5ddccc1">remitted</Substitution>, or the payment terms varied; and</Text></P4para></P4></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d" id="rule-30.5-2-d"><Pnumber>d</Pnumber><P3para><Text>if the application is to remit a criminal courts charge, explain—</Text><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d/i" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d/i" id="rule-30.5-2-d-i"><Pnumber>i</Pnumber><P4para><Text>how the circumstances meet the time limits and other conditions in section 50 of the Sentencing Act 2020<FootnoteRef Ref="f00734"/>, and</Text></P4para></P4><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d/ii" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/d/ii" id="rule-30.5-2-d-ii"><Pnumber>ii</Pnumber><P4para><Text>why the charge should be remitted.</Text></P4para></P4></P3para></P3></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3" id="rule-30.5-3"><Pnumber>3</Pnumber><P2para><Text>The court may determine an application—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3/a" id="rule-30.5-3-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text>at a hearing, which may be in public or in private; or</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/3/b" id="rule-30.5-3-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text>without a hearing.</Text></P3para></P3></P2para></P2><Text><Emphasis>[Note. See sections 75, 85 and 85A of the Magistrates’ Courts Act 1980</Emphasis><FootnoteRef Ref="f00735"/><Emphasis> and sections 50 and 127 of the Sentencing Act 2020.</Emphasis></Text></P1para><P1para><Text><Emphasis>Under section 46 of the 2020 Act, a court must, at the times listed in sections 44 and 45 of that Act, order a defendant convicted of an offence to pay a charge in respect of relevant court costs. Under section 50 of the Act, a magistrates’ court may remit the whole or part of such a charge, but</Emphasis>—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a" id="rule-30.5-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text><Emphasis>the court may do so only if it is satisfied that—</Emphasis></Text><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a/i" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a/i" id="rule-30.5-a-i"><Pnumber>i</Pnumber><P4para><Text><Emphasis>the defendant has taken all reasonable steps to pay the charge, having regard to his or her personal circumstances, or</Emphasis></Text></P4para></P4><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a/ii" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/a/ii" id="rule-30.5-a-ii"><Pnumber>ii</Pnumber><P4para><Text><Emphasis>collection and enforcement of the charge is impracticable;</Emphasis></Text></P4para></P4></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/b" id="rule-30.5-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text><Emphasis>the court may not do so at a time when the defendant is in prison; and</Emphasis></Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/c" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/c" id="rule-30.5-c"><Pnumber>c</Pnumber><P3para><Text><Emphasis>the court may not do so unless the periods specified by regulations under section 21E all have expired.]</Emphasis></Text></P3para></P3></P1para></P1></P1group></Part></Body></Secondary><Footnotes><Footnote id="f00734"><FootnoteText><Para><Text><Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2020/17" id="c02490" Year="2020" Number="17" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2020 c. 17</Citation>.</Text></Para></FootnoteText></Footnote><Footnote id="f00735"><FootnoteText><Para><Text><Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1980/43" id="c02491" Year="1980" Number="43" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1980 c. 43</Citation>; section 75 was amended by section 11 of, and paragraph 6 of Schedule 2 to, the Maintenance Enforcement Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1991/17" id="c02492" Year="1991" Number="17" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1991 (c. 17)</Citation>. Section 85 was substituted by section 61 of the Criminal Justice Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1988/33" id="c02493" Year="1988" Number="33" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1988 (c. 33)</Citation> and amended by section 55 of, and paragraph 10(2) of Schedule 4 to, the Crime (Sentences) Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1997/43" id="c02494" Year="1997" Number="43" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1997 (c. 43)</Citation>, section 109(1) of, and paragraph 222 of Schedule 8 to, the Courts Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2003/39" id="c02495" Year="2003" Number="39" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2003 (c. 39)</Citation> and section 179 of the Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2014/12" id="c02496" Year="2014" Number="12" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2014 (c. 12)</Citation>. It is further amended by paragraphs 25 and 28 of Schedule 32 to the Criminal Justice Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2003/44" id="c02497" Year="2003" Number="44" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2003 (c. 44)</Citation> and section 26 of the Crime and Courts Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2013/22" id="c02498" Year="2013" Number="22" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2013 (c. 22)</Citation>, with effect from dates to be appointed. Section 85A was inserted by section 51(1) of the Criminal Justice Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1982/48" id="c02499" Year="1982" Number="48" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1982 (c. 48)</Citation>.</Text></Para></FootnoteText></Footnote></Footnotes><Commentaries><Commentary id="key-28bc16ac35d32338d54a6afb9d47f6a2" Type="F"><Para><Text>Word in <CitationSubRef id="c5drfl606-00006" SectionRef="rule-30.5" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5">rule 30.5</CitationSubRef> heading substituted (6.4.2026) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47" id="c5drfl606-00007" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2026" Number="47" Title="The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026">The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026 (S.I. 2026/47)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00007" id="c5drfl606-00008" SectionRef="rule-3" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/3">rules 3</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00007" id="c5drfl606-00009" SectionRef="rule-8-a" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/8/a" Operative="true">8(a)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-5f8f9fe45bfb0867d2fb21f0b5ddccc1" Type="F"><Para><Text>Word in <CitationSubRef id="c5drfl606-00034" SectionRef="rule-30.5-2-c-ii" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c/ii">rule 30.5(2)(c)(ii)</CitationSubRef> substituted (6.4.2026) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47" id="c5drfl606-00035" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2026" Number="47" Title="The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026">The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026 (S.I. 2026/47)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00035" id="c5drfl606-00036" SectionRef="rule-3" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/3">rules 3</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00035" id="c5drfl606-00037" SectionRef="rule-8-c-ii" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/8/c/ii" Operative="true">8(c)(ii)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a888c5a3fb73f175f11ab7629ff3c204" Type="F"><Para><Text>Word in <CitationSubRef id="c5drfl606-00025" SectionRef="rule-30.5-2-c" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/2/c">rule 30.5(2)(c)</CitationSubRef> substituted (6.4.2026) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47" id="c5drfl606-00026" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2026" Number="47" Title="The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026">The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026 (S.I. 2026/47)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00026" id="c5drfl606-00027" SectionRef="rule-3" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/3">rules 3</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00026" id="c5drfl606-00028" SectionRef="rule-8-c-i" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/8/c/i" Operative="true">8(c)(i)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-c9768c7929b875915d09db3ebc028657" Type="I"><Para><Text><CitationSubRef id="cy19ybfz5-02583" SectionRef="rule-30.5" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5">Rule 30.5</CitationSubRef> in force at 6.10.2025, see <CitationSubRef id="cy19ybfz5-02584" CitationRef="" SectionRef="introduction" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2025/909/introduction" Operative="true">Preamble</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-dcd87f3e7dc331cc0b2b50f788b4695a" Type="F"><Para><Text><CitationSubRef id="c5drfl606-00016" SectionRef="rule-30.5-1" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/909/rule/30.5/1">Rule 30.5(1)</CitationSubRef>  substituted (6.4.2026) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47" id="c5drfl606-00017" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2026" Number="47" Title="The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026">The Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Rules 2026 (S.I. 2026/47)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00017" id="c5drfl606-00018" SectionRef="rule-3" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/3">rules 3</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c5drfl606-00017" id="c5drfl606-00019" SectionRef="rule-8-b" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2026/47/rule/8/b" Operative="true">8(b)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary></Commentaries></Legislation>